{
  "pack": "common-people",
  "version": 3,
  "stage": "initial",
  "disclaimer": "This pack was prepared by artificial intelligence (AI). It is an initial version: its rules may contain errors and will change as accountants, tax advisers and auditors review them.",
  "history": [
    {
      "versions": "3",
      "date": "2026-10-20",
      "changes": "Who may do what, as data: a role is a named set of rights; a membership puts a person in a company with a role between two dates; a mandate lets an office keep a client's books within a scope of rights; a substitution hands a person's rights to a deputy between two dates; a group names a set of people for a supervisor's reach. The pack's roles: owner, chief accountant, accountant, reader, support. The view that shows who can do what, every right opening to the grant that gives it."
    },
    {
      "versions": "2",
      "date": "2026-10-15",
      "changes": "A person can say their given name, family name and birth date — what a natural person's tax return needs."
    },
    {
      "versions": "1",
      "date": "2026-10-10",
      "changes": "The person as master data: who acts, who is assigned work, who stands in when they are away."
    }
  ],
  "description": "People: the person as master data — who acts, who is assigned, who stands in — and who may do what: roles, memberships, mandates, substitutions, groups. Market-neutral; every pack that assigns work builds on it. v3: rights as data (DIRECTION 2026-10-19, People and rights).",
  "warrant": {
    "basis": "practice",
    "citations": [
      "every ERP keeps the people who use it as master data: a user with a role, and a substitute for absence (SAP workflow substitutes, Comarch operators)",
      "every event in Rhea already names its actor; a person is that actor as an object, so cases, notifications and disputes can refer to a human the way documents refer to a contractor",
      "KSeF 2.0's rights ladder: the taxpayer holds every right, grants named rights to people and to an authorised entity (the accounting office) with or without the right to pass them on; the office grants its employees rights in the client's context — Rhea's membership, mandate and role are those three",
      "the right to manage rights is never implied by the right to do the work (KSeF: zarządzanie uprawnieniami is its own grant): a wildcard over doors stops at the people domain"
    ],
    "scope": "all markets"
  },
